# Add project specific R8 rules here.
# AGP will combine all keep rule files in src/main/keepRules to pass to R8
#
# For more details, see
#   https://d.android.com/r/tools/r8/keep-rules

# If your project uses WebView with JS, uncomment the following
# and specify the fully qualified class name to the JavaScript interface
# class:
#-keepclassmembers class fqcn.of.javascript.interface.for.webview {
#   public *;
#}

# kotlinx-serialization already ships its own consumer R8 rules (verified in
# app/build/outputs/mapping/*/configuration.txt) that keep $$serializer classes and the
# serializer() lookup for every @Serializable type in this app — no extra rules needed here.

# Firebase Realtime Database is only ever read/written here as primitives (String/Boolean/Long)
# and plain Map<String, Any> payloads, via DataSnapshot#getValue(Class) — never bean-mapped into
# our own data classes — so no custom Firebase model keep rules are needed either.

# AccessibilityService, Services, and the FileProvider are declared in AndroidManifest.xml and
# are already kept automatically by the default Android R8 rules (every manifest-declared
# component is kept), so nothing app-specific is required for the update-installer or
# accessibility-bridge flows.